    "headline": "Beach Hazards Statement issued October 13 at 9:29PM PDT until October 15 at 2:00PM PDT by NWS San Diego CA",
    "description": "* WHAT...Elevated high tides 6.5 to 7 ft will continue through\nThursday with surf of 3 to 6 ft with sets to 7 ft expected.\n\n* WHERE...San Diego County Coastal Areas and Orange County\nCoastal Areas.\n\n* WHEN...Through Thursday afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor coastal flooding and beach erosion.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...High tides will fall below 6.5 ft after\nthe Thursday high tide. A south swell from 190 degrees of 3 ft\nwith a 15 to 17 second period will be present through\nThursday. A moderate period, persistent south swell from 190\nwill continue into next week.",
